# 🧠 RAG_WORKFLOW — How CampusGenie Finds Answers (In Depth)

> This document explains **exactly** how the CampusGenie RAG (Retrieval-Augmented
> Generation) pipeline works — end to end, with **real worked examples** using
> actual code paths, constants, and data from the live project.
>
> Two questions are answered in depth:
> 1. **"How does the AI chatbot find an answer?"** — from the moment a student
>    types a message to the moment a cited answer appears.
> 2. **"What happens internally when an admin uploads a document?"** — the full
>    ingestion pipeline from file bytes to searchable vector chunks.
>
> All numbers (chunk sizes, weights, thresholds, model names) are the real values
> in `backend/ai_engine/core/config.py` and the agent code.

