## 1. RAG in One Picture

RAG = **Retrieve** relevant knowledge first, then let the LLM **Generate** an
answer *grounded* in what was retrieved. The LLM is never asked to "know"
anything — it is handed evidence (document chunks + live DB data) and told to
answer **only from that evidence**, citing exact source filenames.

```mermaid
flowchart LR
    KB[(Knowledge Base\nChromaDB · 384-dim vectors)] --> R[RETRIEVE\nfind most relevant chunks]
    DB[(MySQL\nlive student/faculty data)] --> T[TOOL CALLS\nlive data for the user]
    R --> C[CONTEXT\nchunks + tool results + history]
    T --> C
    C --> G[GENERATE\nLLM answers from context only]
    G --> A["Answer + confidence\n+ citations + follow-ups"]
```

The contract: **no hallucination**. Rule 3 of the RAG prompt forbids inventing
dates, marks, percentages, deadlines, names, phone numbers, room numbers, or fee
amounts. If nothing relevant is retrieved, the bot says it doesn't know — but
only as a **last resort** (rule 12) — *any* partial grounding must be answered
from.

